# PhotoPipeline M2-T1 — LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Consumed through the environment (nothing in CMakeLists points at it, so the
# dev/CI command line owns the wiring):
#
#   LSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/tools/lsan.supp:print_suppressions=0" \
#   ASAN_OPTIONS="detect_leaks=1:halt_on_error=0" \
#   UBSAN_OPTIONS="print_stacktrace=1" \
#   build/m2-t1/photopipeline --dev tests/golden/base/* --out /tmp/out --format jxl --workers 2
#
# Verdict for M2-T1: NO ACTIVE SUPPRESSION RULES. This file is intentionally
# comment-only. The whole-corpus ASan/UBSan matrix (base x 8 formats, metadata-only
# x 4 formats, edge/ and meta/ negative corpora x 8 formats, plus the supplementary
# option-axis sweep) produced zero LeakSanitizer reports, so there is nothing to
# suppress and adding rules here would only mask future regressions.
#
# Why the anticipated third-party static-lifetime allocations do not need rules:
# lcms2 (cmsCreate_sRGBProfile / cmsCreateRGBProfile / cmsBuildParametricToneCurve
# caches), OpenImageIO (plugin/attribute registries), Exiv2 (XmpParser registry) and
# libheif (encoder descriptors) all keep their one-shot allocations reachable from
# live globals until process exit. LSan only reports *unreachable* blocks, so these
# process-lifetime singletons are not reported and are accepted as static lifetime
# (M2 task book §4 T1 leak policy). The two in-tree process-lifetime owners are
# pp::ColorManager::Impl (src/core/colormanager.cpp, deliberate per its NOTE) and the
# generated-ICC byte cache; both stay reachable through their function-local statics.
#
# Rule format when one is ever genuinely needed (LSan "leak:" matcher, matched
# against the allocation stack's function/module names), one rule per line with a
# comment stating the evidence that the allocation is a one-shot static:
#   leak:<function or library>
#
# Reproduce the clean result:
#   bash .cache/tmp/m2t1_matrix.sh <label> build/m2-t1     # required matrix
#   bash .cache/tmp/m2t1_supp.sh   <label> build/m2-t1     # supplementary axes
# and confirm the sanitizer channel is live (control must report, then be silent):
#   LD_PRELOAD=.cache/tmp/leakctl.so \
#   ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:verify_asan_link_order=0 \
#   build/m2-t1/photopipeline --dev tests/golden/base/rgb8.png --out /tmp/probe \
#   --format png --workers 2      # => "ERROR: LeakSanitizer: detected memory leaks"
